From: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/ttm: use 0 instead of EMPTY_VMA_FLAGS for older kernels

EMPTY_VMA_FLAGS was introduced in v7.0. For older kernels, shmem_file_setup
accepts a plain flag value of 0 for the equivalent meaning.

Signed-off-by: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_tt.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_tt.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_tt.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_tt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_tt.c
@@ -329,7 +329,11 @@ int ttm_tt_swapout(struct ttm_device *bdev, struct ttm_tt *ttm, gfp_t gfp_flags)
 	struct page *to_page;
 	int i, ret;
 
+#ifdef BPM_EMPTY_VMA_FLAGS_NOT_PRESENT
+	swap_storage = shmem_file_setup("ttm swap", size, 0);
+#else
 	swap_storage = shmem_file_setup("ttm swap", size, EMPTY_VMA_FLAGS);
+#endif
 	if (IS_ERR(swap_storage)) {
 		pr_err("Failed allocating swap storage\n");
 		return PTR_ERR(swap_storage);
-- 
2.34.1
